{
  "_about": "ESMFold2 protein-ligand cocrystal parity, the leg that answers whether the ttnn port folds a co-fold and puts the ligand in the right pocket. Same harness as every other esmfold2 row (scripts/esmfold2_e2e_parity.py), plus the ligand-placement metrics that row cannot carry: pLDDT/distogram/coordinates are dominated by the L^2 protein block and barely move if the ligand ends up in solvent. Target PDB 1FKG (FKBP12 107 aa + SB3), examples/fkg_ligand.yaml, 140 tokens. The protein-only entry is the control: same protein, no ligand, 107 tokens, and slightly WORSE on every parity metric, so the ligand costs no parity. The nucleic entry is a path check at reduced settings (1 recycle, 20 steps) on an arbitrary DNA duplex, not an accuracy claim. Pocket scores come from scripts/esmfold2_ligand_pocket.py against the deposited 1FKG; its controls are 0.000 A / recall 1.0 for identical files and exactly 30.000 A / recall 0.0 for a 30 A displaced ligand.",
